WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.214
Mila is one of three Canadian
research institutes in AI.

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:08.550
And our goal is to be a global pole
for scientific advances

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:12.387
that inspires innovation and the development
of AI for the benefit of all.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:17.893
Mila is a community of a thousand people.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.229
So to make that work, you need
some shared values.

00:00:20.354 --> 00:00:24.733
Some of the core values that are shared here
are around rigour, excellence,

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:28.862
collaboration, innovation, diversity,
inclusion and many more.

00:00:28.987 --> 00:00:32.282
There are four main pillars
to what we do and who we are at Mila.

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:36.036
The first, which is really the core and
the genesis of Mila, is talent.

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:41.458
So attracting, retaining, training talent
that will have a broad...

00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:43.585
spectrum of competencies in AI.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.338
The second is scientific research,
scientific advances,

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:49.299
developing the science's technology
and doing it

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:53.512
really with standards that are shared
at a global scale.

00:00:53.637 --> 00:00:56.807
The third piece is the adoption of AI.
Now, this gets interesting.

00:00:56.932 --> 00:00:59.518
So how do we go from lab to enterprise?

00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:02.145
From kind of the theoretic world
to the real world.

00:01:02.271 --> 00:01:06.316
And here we talk about small enterprises,
start-ups, large organizations,

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:09.820
how do we partner with them
to facilitate that transfer?

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:12.072
And the fourth pillar is social influence.

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:16.243
It's this collective conversation we're in
around what is AI?

00:01:16.368 --> 00:01:18.078
What role should AI play?

00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:21.707
How do we develop AI in a socially
responsible and ethical way?

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:25.627
We need to remember
that this success we have today,

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.380
this institute we have today that
we're so proud of

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:32.384
really rests on decades of work and
on the shoulders of giants.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:35.596
And so, part of what we need to do
is preserve this advantage,

00:01:35.721 --> 00:01:39.183
preserve these bases, right?
But then, as we do that,

00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:44.188
start identifying certain areas, certain domains
where AI can really make a big difference.

00:01:44.313 --> 00:01:46.940
We think about health,
we think about the climate crisis.

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:51.195
And so, as these opportunities emerge,
how are we gonna capture them

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.531
and really allow AI
to realize its full potential?

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:58.493
The Canadian AI ecosystem is
incredibly healthy today.

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:00.579
When you look at some of these
global indexes,

00:02:00.704 --> 00:02:04.082
Canada actually is fourth behind
China, the US and the UK.

00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:06.585
So we're in a good position right now.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:10.005
Part of what we need to do is make sure
that we consolidate that position,

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:15.469
that we don't lose track of the fundamentals
that have allowed us to have all of this success

00:02:15.594 --> 00:02:19.264
and that we continue to do very,
very well what we were most known for.

00:02:19.389 --> 00:02:22.643
And I think that's gonna be important,
part of it is gonna be talent,

00:02:22.768 --> 00:02:24.520
part of it is gonna be investment,

00:02:24.645 --> 00:02:28.732
part of it is gonna be a larger group of
enterprises, small, medium, large,

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:32.903
really taking on AI and understanding
what it needs for them.

00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:37.658
And us collectively in Canada
and in Quebec certainly, deciding:

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:39.952
Okay, what do we want to do
with this AI potential?

00:02:40.077 --> 00:02:42.412
How far are we willing to go?

